id: pm-gh1369
title: "GH-1369: Agent UX: claim --start bypasses compact mutation receipts and returns a noncanonical outer ID"
description: "Reported agent-facing contract defect imported from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1369. Preserve existing shipped foundations. Detailed source observations are dated 2026-09-30 and must be revalidated before implementation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: gh-1369,github-intake,sdk-first
created_at: "2026-10-02T17:09:35.291Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T15:10:09.962Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-03T12:45:11.033Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-03T12:45:11.033Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Short and canonical input IDs produce the same canonical outer ID; Default receipt has final status and changed-field count without duplicate item bodies; Start success, already-owned/no-op, unavailable claim, and update-after-claim failure report truthful stage outcomes; Full-detail opt-in is complete and consistent with the compact receipt; JSON and default rendering share the same semantics; Deterministic payload-size regression catches duplicate snapshot reintroduction; byte counts are not presented as provider tokens"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "SDK lifecycle compositions derive canonical identity from persisted claim/update/close results, preserve full typed SDK constituents and expose compact CLI/MCP receipts with truthful stage outcomes. Repeated-start regression protection excludes both claim and update item snapshots; the historical recurrence lineage has executable registered checks."
expected_result: Claim --start returns a compact canonical ID and final status with changed-field count and truthful stage outcomes by default; detailed snapshots require explicit opt-in and partial failures remain visible.
actual_result: "Final corrected-source isolated suite: 9638 passed and two Windows-only cases skipped on Linux; exact coverage 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (66545/66545 statements, 50900/50900 branches, 13748/13748 functions, 63447/63447 lines). Full type checking, every static-quality stage including unchanged performance ceilings, graph/history and mutation controls (329 killed, seven reviewed equivalent, zero failures), native deduplicated linked tests, 58 clean packed Node/Bun manual commands with history verification, and nine npx/bunx packed package workflows plus typed SDK consumers passed. All 28 touched source functions have behavior-specific documentation. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passed with zero blocking issues, 1.40 percent finish error rate and zero missing error-code rows. Earlier failed test/coverage and performance observations remain recorded. Exact-head hosted checks/reviews and merge follow through PR1376; this batch is separate from the earlier v2026.10.3 publication and four pre-existing-main nightly alerts."
